{"book":54,"chapter":3,"context":{"chapter":3,"title":"Overseers and Deacons","summary":"Paul lists the character qualities required of overseers and deacons, then states his purpose in writing and quotes a short hymn about Christ.","background":"The lists focus almost entirely on character and reputation rather than skills, and resemble lists of virtues Greek writers expected of public leaders. 'The husband of one wife' (v. 2) is variously understood as forbidding polygamy, remarriage or unfaithfulness. Whether v. 11 refers to deacons' wives or to women deacons is also debated.","customs":[{"term":"Bishop (overseer)","verses":"3:1-2","note":"The Greek word means 'overseer', a leader responsible for the care of the local church. In Titus 1:5-7 it seems to describe the same people as 'elders'."}],"watchFor":["A leader must first manage his own household well (vv. 4–5).","The church as 'the pillar and ground of the truth' (v. 15).","Six short lines about Christ, probably an early hymn (v. 16)."],"connections":["Titus 1:5-9","Acts 6:3-6","Acts 20:28","John 1:14"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["Πιστὸς","Pistos","G4103","A-NSM","Trustworthy [is]"],["ὁ","ho","G3588","T-NSM","the"],["λόγος·","logos","G3056","N-NSM","saying"],["εἴ","ei","G1487","COND","If"],["τις","tis","G5100","X-NSM","anyone"],["ἐπισκοπῆς","episkopēs","G1984","N-GSF","overseership"],["ὀρέγεται","oregetai","G3713","V-PMI-3S","aspires to"],["καλοῦ","kalou","G2570","A-GSN","of good"],["ἔργου","ergou","G2041","N-GSN","a work"],["ἐπιθυμεῖ","epithumei","G1937","V-PAI-3S","he is desirous"]],"x":[[56001007,56001007,15],[44020028,44020028,13],[60005002,60005002,8],[60002025,60002025,7],[54001015,54001015,6],[59005019,59005020,6],[42015010,42015010,5],[50001001,50001001,5],[54003002,54003007,5],[54004009,54004009,5]],"xn":19},"2":{"w":[["δεῖ","dei","G1163","V-PAI-3S","It behooves"],["οὖν","oun","G3767","CONJ","therefore"],["τὸν","ton","G3588","T-ASM","the"],["ἐπίσκοπον","episkopon","G1985","N-ASM","overseer"],["ἀνεπίλημπτο